    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d891">

                <pb facs="0924" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg836"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1904</hi></date>,</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 674.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegraphic
                    instruction of March 25 last in relation to the murder of the Rev. B. W.
                    Labaree, an American missionary, in Persia, I have to inform you that the
                    Department is advised by the American minister to Persia, under date of the 8th
                    instant, that Seyid Ghaffar, the murderer of Doctor Labaree, has been captured
                    and incarcerated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. H. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
